concert|music-performance|NOUN|Public musical performance|An occasion when musicians perform music for an audience.|buổi hòa nhạc; buổi biểu diễn âm nhạc|The outdoor concert ended with a song about the sea.|Buổi hòa nhạc ngoài trời kết thúc bằng một bài hát về biển.|Concert is countable; at a concert refers to attendance and in concert can describe a musician performing live.|concert
fifty|number-50|NUMBER|Five tens|The number equal to five groups of ten.|năm mươi; số 50|The volunteers packed fifty lunches for the school trip.|Các tình nguyện viên đóng gói năm mươi phần ăn trưa cho chuyến đi của trường.|Use fifty before a plural count noun for an exact quantity; NUMBER remains a source proposal awaiting taxonomy review.|fifty
ranch|livestock-farm|NOUN|Large livestock farm|A large farm used mainly for raising animals such as cattle or horses.|trang trại chăn nuôi lớn|Two families share the work on this cattle ranch.|Hai gia đình cùng chia sẻ công việc tại trang trại nuôi bò này.|Ranch is countable; on a ranch describes where someone lives or works.|ranch
compare|examine-differences|VERB|Examine similarities and differences|Examine two or more things to find how they are alike and how they differ.|so sánh; đối chiếu điểm giống và khác|We compared the two maps before choosing a walking route.|Chúng tôi so sánh hai bản đồ trước khi chọn tuyến đường đi bộ.|Use compare things or compare one thing with another when examining similarities and differences.|compare
exciting|causes-excitement|ADJECTIVE|Causing enthusiastic interest|Making people feel eager, interested or full of energy.|hào hứng, hấp dẫn; gây hứng thú|The exciting treasure hunt kept the children busy all afternoon.|Cuộc săn tìm kho báu hấp dẫn khiến bọn trẻ bận rộn suốt buổi chiều.|Exciting describes what causes excitement; excited describes the person experiencing it.|exciting
calorie|food-energy-unit|NOUN|Unit for food energy|A unit used to express how much energy food supplies.|calo; đơn vị biểu thị năng lượng thực phẩm|The label shows the number of calories in one serving.|Nhãn ghi số calo trong một khẩu phần.|Calorie is countable; in nutrition, a food calorie commonly represents one kilocalorie, rather than the smaller scientific calorie.|calorie
vegetable|food-plant|NOUN|Plant food for savoury dishes|A plant or part of a plant eaten as food, especially in savoury dishes rather than as fruit or grain.|rau; rau củ dùng làm thực phẩm|The stall sells fresh vegetables from nearby farms.|Quầy hàng bán rau củ tươi từ các trang trại gần đó.|Vegetable is countable when naming an item or kind; vegetables is commonly used for a collection of these foods.|vegetable
teach|give-instruction|VERB|Help someone learn|Give instruction that helps someone learn knowledge or a skill.|dạy; hướng dẫn học kiến thức hoặc kỹ năng|My aunt taught me how to repair a loose button.|Dì tôi đã dạy tôi cách sửa một chiếc cúc bị lỏng.|The forms are teach, taught, taught; use teach a subject, teach someone something or teach someone how to do.|teach
cathedral|principal-church|NOUN|Principal church of a diocese|The main church of a diocese, where a bishop has their official seat.|nhà thờ chính tòa|Visitors admired the stone arches inside the cathedral.|Du khách ngắm những vòm đá bên trong nhà thờ chính tòa.|Cathedral is countable; a church's status, rather than its size alone, makes it a cathedral.|cathedral
garden|planted-area|NOUN|Area for growing plants|An area of land where people grow flowers, vegetables or other plants, often beside a home.|vườn; khu đất trồng cây|Grandfather planted mint along the edge of the garden.|Ông trồng bạc hà dọc theo rìa khu vườn.|Garden is countable; in the garden refers to being within it, while a vegetable garden names its main use.|garden
animal|living-creature|NOUN|Living creature|A living creature such as a mammal, bird, fish or insect, rather than a plant.|động vật|The shelter found homes for several injured animals.|Trung tâm cứu hộ tìm được nơi nuôi dưỡng cho một số động vật bị thương.|Animal is countable; in everyday language it often contrasts with humans, although humans are animals biologically.|animal
tall|large-height|ADJECTIVE|Having considerable height|Having a large distance from the bottom to the top compared with others of the same kind.|cao; có chiều cao lớn|A tall sunflower grew beside the kitchen window.|Một cây hướng dương cao mọc bên cửa sổ bếp.|Use tall for people, trees and upright structures; taller and tallest are the comparison forms.|tall
loaf|bread-piece|NOUN|Bread baked in one piece|Bread shaped and baked as a single piece that can be cut into slices.|ổ bánh mì|Mai sliced a fresh loaf for the picnic.|Mai cắt một ổ bánh mì mới thành lát để mang đi dã ngoại.|The plural is loaves; a loaf of bread counts one complete baked piece.|loaf
skill|learned-ability|NOUN|Ability developed through practice|The ability to do something well, especially through learning and practice.|kỹ năng; sự thành thạo|Repairing the tiny clock required considerable skill.|Sửa chiếc đồng hồ nhỏ xíu đòi hỏi kỹ năng đáng kể.|Use a skill for a particular ability and skill without an article for overall proficiency.|skill
born|come-into-life|VERB|Come into life through birth|Be brought into the world through birth.|được sinh ra; chào đời|My younger sister was born during a summer storm.|Em gái tôi chào đời trong một cơn bão mùa hè.|Use born in be born, such as was born; do not use born as an independent base-form verb.|born
dieter|weight-loss-person|NOUN|Person following a weight-loss diet|A person who follows a particular eating plan in order to lose weight.|người ăn kiêng để giảm cân|The dieter recorded her meals in a small notebook.|Người phụ nữ ăn kiêng để giảm cân ghi lại các bữa ăn trong một cuốn sổ nhỏ.|Dieter is countable and refers to the person, while diet names the eating plan.|dieter
mountain|high-landform|NOUN|Large natural elevation|A large natural rise of land that stands high above the surrounding ground.|núi|Clouds hid the mountain as our bus approached the valley.|Mây che khuất ngọn núi khi xe buýt của chúng tôi đến gần thung lũng.|Mountain is countable; on a mountain names a position on its slopes or summit.|mountain
hat|head-covering|NOUN|Covering worn on the head|An item worn on the head for protection, warmth or appearance.|mũ; vật đội trên đầu|The wind blew Nam's hat into the vegetable patch.|Gió thổi chiếc mũ của Nam vào luống rau.|Hat is countable; wear a hat describes having it on and put on a hat describes the action.|hat
arctic|north-polar-region|NOUN|Northern polar region|The region surrounding the North Pole.|vùng Bắc Cực|The research ship entered the Arctic in July.|Tàu nghiên cứu đi vào vùng Bắc Cực vào tháng Bảy.|Use the Arctic as a geographical noun with a capital A; the source's adjective-like definition requires review against its noun example.|Arctic
apartment|residential-unit|NOUN|Home within a larger building|A set of rooms forming one home inside a larger building.|căn hộ|Their apartment overlooks a narrow canal.|Căn hộ của họ nhìn ra một con kênh hẹp.|Apartment is countable; flat is a common British English equivalent for this residential unit.|apartment
